# Derivation, OPEN WORLD (spec 2026-09-08 §3.4): a document states a corpus reading
# with no date on the CLAIM. Evidence-positive and monotonic — a figure is derived
# only where its support is present: an occurrence exists only where the extractor
# matched the literal to a registered reading (tests/corpus-manifest.ttl), so nothing
# is ever inferred from the absence of a date in the register.
#
# The closed-world half is inside one block and nowhere else: NOT EXISTS over the
# occurrence's own dg:blockDated is holon-scoped closure (CLAUDE.md §8) — the block
# either carries the reading's date or it does not, while the graph stays open.
#
# docs/superpowers/** is EXEMPT: it is the dated historical record, append-only and
# prospectively binding since 5743af3, so a figure there is dated BY THE DOCUMENT.
# That exemption is not free, and [[R192]] carries its price.
PREFIX dg: <https://w3id.org/iladub/docgov#>
CONSTRUCT { ?doc dg:statesUndatedReading ?occ }
WHERE {
    ?occ dg:inDoc          ?doc ;
         dg:denotesReading ?reading ;
         dg:blockDated     false .
    ?doc dg:docClass ?class .
    FILTER (?class != "evidence")
}
